1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:39,160
So that's the largest magical city
in the northern lands, Äußerst.

4
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:41,650
We're still a long ways away.

5
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:44,020
We'll need to hitch a ride on
a carriage on our way there.

6
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,910
Once you get your first-class
mage certification there,

7
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:51,910
we'll be able to enter the Northern Plateau.

8
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:56,750
I don't think I have to be
the one to get certified.

9
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:59,090
I won't be able to use it for long, anyway.

10
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:01,860
You should get certified, Fern.

11
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,910
Ms. Frieren, don't you know?

12
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:11,180
Only a handful of the most skilled mages
have ever gained a first-class certification.

13
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:14,040
I certainly couldn't manage it.

14
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:17,470
Oh, really?

15
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,500
You don't seem interested.

16
00:02:20,290 --> 00:02:21,990
It's a bit late to ask,

17
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:24,150
but why do we need to be accompanied

18
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:26,640
by a crazy-powerful mage to enter
the Northern Plateau, anyway?

19
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:29,410
The Northern Plateau has long been inhabited

20
00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:33,660
by many cunning, magic-using
monsters like the Einsam.

21
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:39,140
It's a dangerous region that you once couldn't
cross without a priest and a skilled mage.

22
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,770
That said, if someone as valuable

23
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:45,410
as a skilled mage is required
to travel through the area,

24
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:49,160
something pretty serious must be
happening on the Northern Plateau.

25
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:55,160
We'll look into the exam
once we arrive in Äußerst.

26
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:58,620
According to Fern, there's a combat test.

27
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:00,980
I'll need to come up with a strategy.

28
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:06,430
Aren't you powerful enough to
easily handle any kind of test?

29
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:08,820
Even when you're suppressing your mana,

30
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,450
you still produce as much
as an experienced old mage.

31
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,550
Don't call me an old mage.

32
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,280
Now she's sulking.

33
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:20,330
Don't you think calling her
an old mage was a bit mean?

34
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:21,910
I'm sorry.

35
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,700
I haven't forgotten that you
called me an old hag, Stark.

36
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,400
How long ago was that?

37
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:30,960
Forget it. I'm going to sleep.

38
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,670
Wake me when we get to Äußerst.

39
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:35,510
Sheesh.

40
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:40,270
Actually, never mind.

41
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:42,170
What's wrong?

42
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:45,170
I could only see half the sky.

43
00:03:46,930 --> 00:03:47,710
What?

44
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:49,940
Just so you know, Fern,

45
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,190
mana isn't the only factor that
determines a mage's strength.

46
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:58,600
Technique, experience, the spells
they use, their control...

47
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,550
There's effort and tenacity, too.

48
00:04:00,550 --> 00:04:02,860
Some of those sound more like warrior traits.

49
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:05,030
Finally, there's talent.

50
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:12,980
In my life, I've lost eleven times to
mages who had less mana than me.

51
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:16,000
Four of them were demons.

52
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,740
Qual was one of them.

53
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:21,620
One was an elf like me,

54
00:04:22,370 --> 00:04:25,290
and the remaining six were humans.

55
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:31,400
The graf's city should be
coming into view soon.

56
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:35,060
The road to Äußerst is steep.

57
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:38,260
Maybe I'll take a break.

58
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:43,000
That's a nice staff you've got there, miss.

59
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:49,490
What's this? More bandits?

60
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:53,370
We're finally enjoying peace now
that Aura has been defeated, too.

61
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:56,610
But now we're seeing more of these types.

62
00:04:56,610 --> 00:04:58,320
Who told you to speak?

63
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,820
Gather your things and—

64
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:08,430
Bastard.

65
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:19,510
If you value your lives,
then leave this place.

66
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:22,450
Let's go.

67
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:27,910
Thanks for saving me.

68
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,910
I'm Übel the Mage.

69
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,020
Kraft the Monk.

70
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,000
Huh? Are you an elf?

71
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,290
How unusual. This is my
first time seeing one.

72
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:42,290
You have the eyes of a killer.

73
00:05:45,410 --> 00:05:47,690
I didn't rescue you.

74
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:52,550
I found the torn-up bodies
of bandits in the woods nearby.

75
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,260
They'd been killed by a mage.

76
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,810
A tremendously skilled one, no less.

77
00:05:58,630 --> 00:05:59,900
Oh, yeah?

78
00:06:01,670 --> 00:06:04,070
Did you come to lecture me?

79
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:08,010
No. I'm an adventurer, too.

80
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:12,060
I'm not so hard-headed as to criticize
someone for killing in self-defense.

81
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,610
I was simply saving the lives
I saw in front of me.

82
00:06:16,090 --> 00:06:19,080
You're a shrewd old man. You're no fun.

83
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,840
Are you headed to Äußerst?

84
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:26,340
Yeah. I'm going to take
the first-class mage exam.

85
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,930
Frieren said the same thing.

86
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:35,810
I look forward to hearing about her
adventures when I see her next.

87
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:39,980
The exam will take place
two months from now.

88
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:45,240
Keep in mind that the first-class mage exam
is administered once every three years.

89
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:51,200
Also, a fifth-class mage or higher
certification is required to take the exam.

90
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,870
Fern, it's all up to you.

91
00:06:57,420 --> 00:07:00,650
Ms. Frieren, I can't do this alone.

92
00:07:00,650 --> 00:07:01,740
Sure you can.

93
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:04,450
What are we going to do if I fail?

94
00:07:04,450 --> 00:07:06,880
The first-class mage exam is only
held once every three years.

95
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:11,260
We'll either hire a first-class mage
or travel by sea.

96
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:14,550
That would be incredibly expensive.

97
00:07:14,550 --> 00:07:17,480
We won't be able to afford snacks anymore.

98
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:22,890
But I'm uncertified.

99
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:30,110
My holy emblem won't work, will it?

100
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,810
Again, what is that antique?

101
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,660
Hey, you.

102
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,630
Could I take a look at that?

103
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:49,340
Are you planning to take
the first-class mage exam?

104
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:54,420
Looks like I get to take the exam.

105
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:58,170
I'm surprised there's anyone around
who still knows what this is.

106
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:01,560
Is that thing impressive?

107
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:04,140
It's supposed to be.

108
00:08:06,970 --> 00:08:10,450
Frieren, you're not part
of a magic guild, are you?

109
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:14,570
The organizations that manage
magic change all the time.

110
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:17,620
I can't be bothered to join every one.

111
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,080
Huh.

112
00:08:20,030 --> 00:08:22,320
Besides, I have this.

113
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:25,530
A holy emblem. Pretty impressive, right?

114
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:30,650
What's this rusty necklace? Any clue?

115
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:31,720
None at all.

116
00:08:37,990 --> 00:08:39,030
I see.

117
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:44,720
But this is the only thing
that proves I'm a mage.

118
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:50,850
Frieren, it's true that we
don't recognize that necklace.

119
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:56,000
But we know you're an incredible mage.

120
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,220
Isn't that enough?

121
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,110
But you'll die so soon.

122
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:10,340
Ms. Frieren.

123
00:09:11,770 --> 00:09:16,880
We know you're an incredible mage.

124
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:23,560
You're right.

125
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:29,140
According to the Continental
Magic Association's regulations,

126
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:34,780
a person becomes a proper mage
once they've achieved at least fifth class.

127
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:37,910
Fern, why did you get a
third-class certification?

128
00:09:38,590 --> 00:09:41,620
Because it had the soonest
available testing date.

129
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:46,740
There are 600 mages who
are at least fifth class.

130
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:51,420
Even when you include apprentices from sixth
to ninth class, there are 2,000 mages total.

131
00:09:51,890 --> 00:09:54,570
Among them, 45 are first class.

132
00:09:54,570 --> 00:09:56,670
The first-class exam is held
once every three years

133
00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:01,920
at the northern branch in Äußerst and the
headquarters in the holy city of Strahl.

134
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:06,220
Many years, no one passes the test at all.

135
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:08,950
Some test-takers are expected
to be injured or die.

136
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,990
It seems moderately challenging.

137
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:16,420
Either way, there are a lot
fewer mages these days.

138
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:18,430
There used to be more?

139
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:22,570
A century ago, when the Demon King's
attacks intensified,

140
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:26,830
you could expect to encounter at least
one mage while walking around town.

141
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:30,590
These days, you hardly see
them outside magic cities.

142
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:36,470
Let's train thoroughly to prepare
for the exam in two months.

143
00:11:08,890 --> 00:11:13,390
The first-class mage exam will now begin.

144
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:18,730
The first-class mage
certification is granted only

145
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:17,010
This year's test-takers
seem rather exceptional.

146
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:21,710
Wirbel, second-class mage and
captain of the Northern Magic Corps

147
00:11:18,730 --> 00:11:21,110
to the most exceptionally
talented and powerful mages.

148
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:24,370
Only a few mages are granted the title.

149
00:11:21,710 --> 00:11:26,020
that has fought against the remnants
of the Demon King's forces for years.

150
00:11:24,370 --> 00:11:27,810
Naturally, the exam is quite dangerous,

151
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:31,920
Denken, the crafty old
second-class mage who won

152
00:11:27,810 --> 00:11:31,950
but the Association will not intervene
regardless of what happens to you.

153
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:36,520
a bloody struggle for power
to become an imperial mage.

154
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:44,290
Fern, the youngest mage to ever receive
a third-class certification with top marks.

155
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:47,280
Of course, there are some
problem children as well.

156
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:52,660
Übel, the third-class mage who failed
the second-class exam two years ago

157
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:56,910
when she killed the first-class mage
who proctored it.

158
00:11:58,410 --> 00:12:00,820
Who else looks promising?

159
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:07,410
I see someone radiating the mana
of an experienced old mage.

160
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:09,400
Who is that?

161
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,560
I don't know.

162
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:15,030
I will now announce the content
of the first test in this exam.

163
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,950
You will be tested as parties.

164
00:12:16,950 --> 00:12:23,010
The 57 exam-takers will split into teams
of three for the first test.

165
00:12:24,170 --> 00:12:26,930
We will now assign parties.

166
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:29,780
<i>Bracelets, huh?</i>

167
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:35,900
<i>They have numbers on them.
I must be in the 2nd party.</i>

168
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:40,920
<i>Imbuing it with mana allows me to locate
the bracelets belonging to my party members.</i>

169
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,330
<i>So this is how we identify
our party members.</i>

170
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:47,080
<i>Either way, this is interesting.</i>

171
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:49,040
<i>Setting aside normal party compositions,</i>

172
00:12:49,910 --> 00:12:56,190
<i>these improvised parties of magical
miscreants will struggle to work together.</i>

173
00:12:57,630 --> 00:13:00,590
<i>First impressions are important here.</i>

174
00:13:00,590 --> 00:13:03,200
<i>I should be careful not to make waves.</i>

175
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:06,700
<i>I sense my party members'
bracelets around here.</i>

176
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:09,500
Ow, ow, ow!

177
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:10,600
You're gonna rip them off!

178
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:13,970
You can't be serious! I'll kill you!

179
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,480
Try it.

180
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,470
<i>They're already fighting.</i>

181
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,120
Nice to meet you.

182
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,940
It's nice to meet you.

183
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:34,850
Allow me to explain the specific
rules of the first test.

184
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:40,140
Small birds known as Stille
live within the testing area.

185
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:44,830
Each party has been given one cage.

186
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:47,640
There are two conditions you must
fulfill to pass the first test.

187
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:52,030
First, by sunset tomorrow,
have a cage containing a Stille,

188
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,280
Stay away from me!

189
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:56,290
and second, have all of your party
members present at that time.

190
00:13:57,930 --> 00:14:00,160
You are mostly free to do as you wish,

191
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:04,170
but if anyone leaves the testing area,

192
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:08,180
their entire party will fail the test.

193
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:12,120
They say that like there isn't a barrier
around the testing area

194
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,920
that won't let so much as
a speck of dust through.

195
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,770
It's not like we <i>can</i> get out.

196
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:20,020
So they're actually listening
to the explanation.

197
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:23,640
The first test begins now.

198
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,420
We should start by coming up with a plan!

199
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:27,640
Are you stupid?

200
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,760
We can't come up with a plan
if we can't even find them!

201
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:33,180
They're still fighting.

202
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:37,610
Why don't we introduce
ourselves while we walk?

203
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:44,710
Also, use rock-paper-scissors to
decide who will carry the cage.

204
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:52,880
I'm Frieren. Nice to meet you.

205
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,890
I'm Lawine, a third-class mage.

206
00:14:56,490 --> 00:14:59,690
I'm Kanne, also a third-class mage.

207
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,450
Lawine and I go way back.

208
00:15:01,450 --> 00:15:03,890
We graduated from the same magic school.

209
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:07,440
Do you two know anything about the Stille?

210
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,190
No.

211
00:15:08,190 --> 00:15:09,150
Nope.

212
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:13,970
I do, but I've never seen
one in person before.

213
00:15:13,970 --> 00:15:17,290
Let's start by finding a
Stille and observing it.

214
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,870
I'm tired.

215
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:42,510
You're so undisciplined.

216
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:44,430
Shall we take a break?

217
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,320
I can keep moving. I'll go ahead
and check things out.

218
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,940
It's safer to stay together.

219
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:55,810
Oh, shut up. That's so inefficient.

220
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,950
Lawine, are you strong?

221
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:00,880
Stronger than her.

222
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:02,210
You wanna fight, huh?

223
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:04,090
And compared to me?

224
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:08,060
I wouldn't want to fight you.

225
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,100
I see.

226
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,200
Fine. Go check things out.

227
00:16:12,590 --> 00:16:15,350
Come back if it gets too dangerous.

228
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:16,080
Okay.

229
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:19,170
And watch the skies.

230
00:16:19,170 --> 00:16:20,450
I know.

231
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:26,050
<i>I wonder if our party will be okay.</i>

232
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,630
Frieren, you're like a teacher.

233
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,370
You'd make a good leader.

234
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,460
It's because you two keep fighting.

235
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:36,110
I don't want to lead.

236
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:40,670
Sorry. We've always been like this.

237
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:44,970
By the way, what did you mean
when you said to watch the skies?

238
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:46,680
I meant exactly what I said.

239
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:49,640
Do you struggle to detect mana?

240
00:16:50,430 --> 00:16:51,760
Why?

241
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,580
Hey.

242
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,090
That was quick.

243
00:16:55,090 --> 00:16:56,560
I found a Stille.

244
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:03,490
Nicely done, Lawine. Now watch it closely.

245
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:11,030
I told you to observe.

246
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,800
It's going to run away.

247
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:15,780
I don't think so. Nice work, Kanne.

248
00:17:20,130 --> 00:17:22,020
Huh. Not bad.

249
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:26,730
But you should probably get down.

250
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:28,910
What? Why?

251
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:36,220
Stille are incredibly tough.

252
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,870
Their top speed is faster
than the speed of sound.

253
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:41,900
Trying to restrain one
like that is pointless.

254
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:45,370
Seriously? It's already gone.

255
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:46,670
That was close.

256
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:49,740
Capturing one will require
careful observation.

257
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:53,110
We'll use this entire day
for Stille observation.

258
00:17:54,390 --> 00:17:59,120
<i>Kanne controlled the water,
and Lawine froze it.</i>

259
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:02,200
<i>Their timing was perfectly coordinated.</i>

260
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,030
<i>Their teamwork is superb.</i>

261
00:18:04,030 --> 00:18:06,910
<i>It's not something you
could achieve overnight.</i>

262
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:11,530
<i>I was worried for a while there,
but this might actually work.</i>

263
00:18:11,530 --> 00:18:12,810
Let's go after it.

264
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:16,780
We should search around the lake instead.

265
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:19,380
Why? We should go sooner rather than later.

266
00:18:17,810 --> 00:18:20,870
<i>Nope. They're fighting again.</i>

267
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:53,410
I hear something. Huh?

268
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:57,510
Frieren's missing.

269
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:05,150
It's faint, but that's the sound of rain.

270
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:13,530
But it's not raining, so why...?

271
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:17,030
Oh, I see.

272
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:19,000
Does that mean...?

273
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:23,780
A monster!

274
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:35,250
My staff...

275
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:40,500
Lawine!

276
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:54,140
I told you to watch the skies.

277
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:05,700
Have you calmed down?

278
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:07,200
Yeah.

279
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:10,400
You called Lawine's name.

280
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,010
But you don't like Lawine, do you?

281
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,570
No, I don't.

282
00:20:18,310 --> 00:20:22,890
Right? So how do you two
work together so well?

283
00:20:23,370 --> 00:20:24,470
It's strange.

284
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:28,900
I'm surprisingly craven.

285
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:33,900
I often fail to act during critical moments.

286
00:20:36,530 --> 00:20:40,310
It happened when I cast
my first flying spell, too.

287
00:20:42,990 --> 00:20:47,030
The ones who already left
are already so far away.

288
00:20:47,030 --> 00:20:49,860
You'll have water beneath you,
so it's not like you'll die.

289
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:53,600
If you don't have the courage
to do it, want me to kick you?

290
00:20:53,970 --> 00:20:55,910
I hate you, Lawine.

291
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:57,790
I know.

292
00:20:58,490 --> 00:21:01,490
You're always so mean to me.

293
00:21:01,490 --> 00:21:05,260
I'm the kind of person who
grows with praise, you know.

294
00:21:05,810 --> 00:21:07,590
You're joking, right?

295
00:21:07,590 --> 00:21:11,920
This is what happens when you grow up
babied by a kind mommy and daddy.

296
00:21:12,470 --> 00:21:15,910
If it'll help you fly,
I'll be as nice as you want.

297
00:21:17,030 --> 00:21:19,450
Then name my strengths.

298
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:22,310
Are you for real?

299
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:31,260
You try really hard even
though you're a coward.

300
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:32,030
What?

301
00:21:33,710 --> 00:21:35,820
That's your strength.

302
00:21:38,190 --> 00:21:39,450
Tell me more.

303
00:21:39,450 --> 00:21:41,370
What? Why?

304
00:21:43,570 --> 00:21:46,720
You work really hard in secret.

305
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,550
You're considerate and pay attention
to your surroundings.

306
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:52,090
More.

307
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:58,230
You're cute when you smile.

308
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,140
What? Ew.

309
00:22:06,570 --> 00:22:08,410
That was close.

310
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:11,840
So you can fly after all.

311
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,410
I'm done being kind to you.

312
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:19,540
Lawine is rough, but she
pulls me along with her.

313
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:23,040
Because of her, I realized
I can manage most things

314
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:25,540
if I just go for it, even if I'm scared.

315
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:30,520
By the way, Frieren...

316
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:36,140
I noticed something interesting.

317
00:22:40,710 --> 00:22:43,370
Do you think this could be useful?

318
00:22:44,090 --> 00:22:45,030
I see.

319
00:22:45,390 --> 00:22:49,150
We might be able to capture
a Stille easily after all.

320
00:24:20,420 --> 00:24:21,700
It's strange.

321
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:22,750
Let's do this.

322
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:23,920
Why are you so relaxed?

323
00:24:22,750 --> 00:24:23,900
They're inexperienced.

324
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:24,890
Someone's detected us.

325
00:24:23,910 --> 00:24:25,790
It's time to fight other mages.

326
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:25,790
Shut up.

327
00:24:24,870 --> 00:24:27,370
Then there's no need for words.

328
00:24:25,790 --> 00:24:29,860
This is the 2nd party's well-laid plan.
